정책 의존은 사슬이고 순환이 없습니다: `org_members ← studies ← applications ← (briefs, slots, notes, messages, rewards)`.

## 4. 핵심 흐름

| 흐름 | 라우트 | 메모 |
|---|---|---|
| 옆자리로 시작하기 | `GET /auth/yeopjari/start` → yeopjari → `/auth/yeopjari/callback` | 진행 중 로그인은 봉인 쿠키 `yi_sso`(DB 없음). 같은 `sub` → 확인된 같은 이메일의 기존 계정(담당자가 참여자도 되는 경우) → 새 계정. 처음이면 `/start`로. 회사 인증은 로그인마다 옆자리를 따름 |
| 담당자 로그인 | `POST /auth/code/request` → `/auth/code/verify` | 등록 여부와 관계없이 같은 답. 틀린 코드는 401이지만 시도 횟수는 커밋(응답을 던지지 않고 반환) |
| 참여 프로필 | `GET/PUT /participant`, `POST /participant/pause` | 처음 완성할 때만 `draft → active`(가드 트리거, 서비스 단계) |
| 연구 목록·안내 | `GET /studies`, `/studies/:id` | 공개. 로그인한 참여자에게는 `fit`(충족·미충족 사유) |
| 신청 | `POST /studies/:id/apply` | 조건 판정(domain/eligibility.ts) → 사전 질문 판정(탈락 규칙은 elevate로만 읽음) → 코드명 → INSERT(RLS `can_apply`) |
| 선정·완료 | `POST /team/applications/:id/decision` | 상태 전이는 가드 트리거가 허용한 것만. 완료하면 보상 행(받을 곳 있으면 `ready`) |
| 일정 | `POST /participations/:id/slot` | 새 자리 증가·옛 자리 감소·신청 갱신을 한 문장으로, 하나라도 어긋나면 롤백 |
| 제출 | `POST /participations/:id/submit` | 선정 상태에서만, 완료 확인 전까지 다시 제출 가능 |
| 보상 | `PUT /participant/payout`, `/admin/rewards/*` | 받을 곳 봉인, 운영자 열람은 건별·감사 기록, 지급 완료는 묶음 |
| 연구 검수 | `POST /team/studies/:id/submit` → `POST /admin/studies/:id/review` | 공개는 운영자만(가드 트리거). 공개 뒤 보상·조건·사전 질문은 잠김 |
| 예상 인원 | `POST /team/studies/:id/reach` | `insight_priv.fits()`로 센다(elevate, 숫자만, 5명 단위·5명 미만은 "미만") |
| 결과 요약 | `GET /team/studies/:id/results` | 사전 질문은 신청자 전체(취소 제외), 제출 양식은 제출자. 선택지 수·평균·서술형(코드명과) |
| 캘린더 | `GET /participations/:id/calendar.ics`, `GET /team/studies/:id/calendar.ics` | UTC, RFC 5545 이스케이프·75바이트 접기(`util/ics.ts`) |
| 지급 목록 | `POST /admin/rewards/export` | 지급 대기 + 받을 곳을 연 CSV, AAL2, 감사 기록에 보상 ID 전부 |
| 사이트맵·미리보기 | `GET /sitemap.xml`, Function `studyPreview` | 공개 연구만. 미리보기는 비회원으로 읽어 엣지 5분 |

## 5. 배치 (`routes/internal.ts`, 10분)

세션·코드·쿼터 정리, 감사 기록 1년·문의 1년 보관 뒤 삭제, 회사 인증 만료, 마감일 지난 모집 → 진행 중,
제출 뒤 7일 확인 없는 비동기 과제 자동 완료 + 보상, **새 연구 알림**(참여자마다 `participant.alert_days`에 한 번, 마지막 알림 이후
공개되고 `fits`가 참이며 아직 신청 안 한 연구를 한 메일로, 보내기 전에 시각을 찍어 중복 없음), **선정 뒤 미진행 알림**(2일, 한 번),
세션 24시간 전 참여자 알림, 세션 끝나고 24시간 표시 없으면 기업 알림,
탈퇴 7일 뒤 계정 삭제(미지급 보상 취소, 신청·지급 기록은 계정 없이 코드명으로 남음).

## 6. 검증 게이트

`npm run check`(단위 40), `node scripts/e2e.mjs`(151), `node scripts/screenshots.mjs`(85장, 콘솔 오류·5xx·가로 넘침 0).
배포 후 `scripts/smoke-prod.mjs`가 공개 화면·헤더·가드레일을 확인하고, yeopjari 점검 계정(`YEOPJARI_SMOKE_*`)으로
**실제 옆자리 OAuth 왕복**을 해서 세션을 받아 본 뒤 그 계정을 synthetic으로 표시합니다.

/**
 * API client (the same shape as yeopjari's).
 *
 * One place that knows how this backend speaks: same-origin cookies, the CSRF
 * token echoed from its companion cookie, and the single error shape every
 * route returns. Screens get a typed error with field messages they can put
 * next to the input that caused them.
 */
import { invalidateAll, remember, takeEarly } from './cache'

export interface FieldErrors {
  [field: string]: string
}

export class ApiError extends Error {
  readonly status: number
  readonly code: string
  readonly fieldErrors: FieldErrors
  readonly detail: Record<string, unknown>
  readonly requestId: string
  readonly retryAfter: number | null

  constructor(init: {
    status: number
    code: string
    message: string
    fieldErrors?: FieldErrors
    detail?: Record<string, unknown>
    requestId?: string
    retryAfter?: number | null
  }) {
    super(init.message)
    this.name = 'ApiError'
    this.status = init.status
    this.code = init.code
    this.fieldErrors = init.fieldErrors ?? {}
    this.detail = init.detail ?? {}
    this.requestId = init.requestId ?? ''
    this.retryAfter = init.retryAfter ?? null
  }

  /** True when the member simply needs to sign in again. */
  get isUnauthenticated(): boolean {
    return this.status === 401
  }

  /** True when retrying the same request could succeed. */
  get isRetryable(): boolean {
    return this.status === 429 || this.status === 503 || this.status >= 500
  }
}

export const CSRF_HEADER = 'x-insight-csrf'

/**
 * Tells the server which session this call is about. Both the member app and
 * the admin console can be signed in at once - possibly as different accounts -
 * so without this the server answers "who am I" with whichever cookie it
 * happens to check first.
 */
export const SESSION_HINT_HEADER = 'x-insight-session'

function isAdminSurface(): boolean {
  return window.location.pathname.startsWith('/admin')
}

type Listener = (error: ApiError) => void
const unauthenticatedListeners = new Set<Listener>()

/**
 * Notified when any call comes back unauthenticated, so the shell can move to
 * the sign-in screen once instead of every screen handling it.
 */
export function onUnauthenticated(listener: Listener): () => void {
  unauthenticatedListeners.add(listener)
  return () => unauthenticatedListeners.delete(listener)
}

const degradedListeners = new Set<() => void>()

/**
 * Notified when the service says its database is out of reach (503
 * db_unavailable) or answers from a saved copy (x-insight-stale), so the
 * shell shows one notice instead of every screen an error of its own - and a
 * member whose "who am I" failed is told why they look signed out.
 */
export function onServiceDegraded(listener: () => void): () => void {
  degradedListeners.add(listener)
  return () => degradedListeners.delete(listener)
}

function reportDegraded(): void {
  for (const listener of degradedListeners) listener()
}

function readCookie(name: string): string {
  for (const part of document.cookie.split(';')) {
    const eq = part.indexOf('=')
    if (eq <= 0) continue
    if (part.slice(0, eq).trim() === name) {
      try {
        return decodeURIComponent(part.slice(eq + 1).trim())
      } catch {
        return ''
      }
    }
  }
  return ''
}

/** The admin console has its own session, so it echoes its own token. */
function csrfToken(): string {
  const admin = isAdminSurface()
  return readCookie(admin ? 'yi_acsrf' : 'yi_csrf')
}

export interface RequestOptions {
  /** Replays a previous result instead of repeating a state change. */
  idempotencyKey?: string
  signal?: AbortSignal
  /** Raw bytes instead of JSON. */
  body?: BodyInit
  contentType?: string
  headers?: Record<string, string>
}

async function request<T>(
  method: string,
  path: string,
  payload?: unknown,
  options: RequestOptions = {},
): Promise<T> {
  const headers: Record<string, string> = { accept: 'application/json', ...options.headers }
  if (isAdminSurface()) headers[SESSION_HINT_HEADER] = 'admin'
  const unsafe = method !== 'GET' && method !== 'HEAD'
  if (unsafe) {
    const token = csrfToken()
    if (token) headers[CSRF_HEADER] = token
  }
  if (options.idempotencyKey) headers['idempotency-key'] = options.idempotencyKey

  let body: BodyInit | undefined
  if (options.body !== undefined) {
    body = options.body
    headers['content-type'] = options.contentType ?? 'application/octet-stream'
  } else if (payload !== undefined) {
    body = JSON.stringify(payload)
    headers['content-type'] = 'application/json'
  }

  let response: Response
  try {
    // A plain read boot.js already started is taken over rather than repeated;
    // if that one failed on the network, ask again here.
    const early = method === 'GET' && !options.headers ? takeEarly(path) : undefined
    const answered = early ? await early.catch(() => null) : null
    response = answered ?? await fetch(path, {
      method,
      headers,
      body,
      // Cookies are same-origin in every deployment; never send them cross-site.
      credentials: 'same-origin',
      signal: options.signal,
    })
  } catch (err) {
    if (err instanceof DOMException && err.name === 'AbortError') throw err
    throw new ApiError({
      status: 0,
      code: 'network',
      message: '네트워크에 연결할 수 없습니다. 연결 상태를 확인한 뒤 다시 시도해 주세요.',
    })
  }

  if (response.status === 204) return undefined as T

  const text = await response.text()
  let parsed: unknown = null
  if (text) {
    try {
      parsed = JSON.parse(text)
    } catch {
      parsed = null
    }
  }

  if (!response.ok) {
    const envelope = (parsed ?? {}) as {
      error?: { code?: string; message?: string; field_errors?: FieldErrors; detail?: Record<string, unknown> }
      request_id?: string
    }
    const error = new ApiError({
      status: response.status,
      code: envelope.error?.code ?? String(response.status),
      message: envelope.error?.message ?? defaultMessage(response.status),
      fieldErrors: envelope.error?.field_errors,
      detail: envelope.error?.detail,
      requestId: envelope.request_id ?? response.headers.get('x-request-id') ?? '',
      retryAfter: Number(response.headers.get('retry-after')) || null,
    })
    if (error.isUnauthenticated) {
      // Whoever was signed in is not any more; nothing of theirs may be
      // served from memory to whoever signs in next.
      invalidateAll()
      for (const listener of unauthenticatedListeners) listener(error)
    }
    if (error.code === 'db_unavailable') reportDegraded()
    throw error
  }

  if (response.headers.get('x-insight-stale') === '1') reportDegraded()

  // A change this reader made: every cached read may now be out of date, and
  // they must see their own write at once. Writes are rare next to reads, so
  // emptying the whole cache costs little and cannot miss a related key.
  if (unsafe) invalidateAll()

  return parsed as T
}

function defaultMessage(status: number): string {
  if (status === 401) return '로그인이 필요합니다.'
  if (status === 403) return '권한이 없습니다.'
  if (status === 404) return '대상을 찾을 수 없습니다.'
  if (status === 413) return '보낸 내용이 너무 큽니다.'
  if (status === 429) return '요청이 많습니다. 잠시 후 다시 시도해 주세요.'
  if (status >= 500) return '서버에 문제가 발생했습니다. 잠시 후 다시 시도해 주세요.'
  return '요청을 처리할 수 없습니다.'
}

/**
 * A state-changing request whose answer is a file (the payout list): the same
 * headers as any write, the body saved under the server's file name.
 */
async function download(path: string, payload: unknown, fallbackName: string): Promise<void> {
  const headers: Record<string, string> = { 'content-type': 'application/json' }
  if (isAdminSurface()) headers[SESSION_HINT_HEADER] = 'admin'
  const token = csrfToken()
  if (token) headers[CSRF_HEADER] = token
  const response = await fetch(path, { method: 'POST', headers, body: JSON.stringify(payload ?? {}), credentials: 'same-origin' })
  if (!response.ok) {
    const envelope = (await response.json().catch(() => ({}))) as { error?: { code?: string; message?: string } }
    throw new ApiError({ status: response.status, code: envelope.error?.code ?? String(response.status), message: envelope.error?.message ?? defaultMessage(response.status) })
  }
  const name = /filename="([^"]+)"/.exec(response.headers.get('content-disposition') ?? '')?.[1] ?? fallbackName
  const url = URL.createObjectURL(await response.blob())
  const link = document.createElement('a')
  link.href = url
  link.download = name
  document.body.appendChild(link)
  link.click()
  link.remove()
  window.setTimeout(() => URL.revokeObjectURL(url), 10_000)
}

export const api = {
  download,
  get: <T>(path: string, options?: RequestOptions) => request<T>('GET', path, undefined, options),
  /**
   * A read that may be answered from memory for up to `maxAge` ms, shared
   * with concurrent callers. See api/cache.ts for when the cache is emptied.
   * Not abortable per caller, since the request may be serving several.
   */
  cached: <T>(path: string, maxAge: number) => remember<T>(path, maxAge, () => request<T>('GET', path)),
  /** Starts a cached read early, for a link the reader is about to open. */
  prefetch: (path: string, maxAge: number) => {
    void remember(path, maxAge, () => request('GET', path)).catch(() => {})
  },
  post: <T>(path: string, payload?: unknown, options?: RequestOptions) =>
    request<T>('POST', path, payload, options),
  put: <T>(path: string, payload?: unknown, options?: RequestOptions) =>
    request<T>('PUT', path, payload, options),
  patch: <T>(path: string, payload?: unknown, options?: RequestOptions) =>
    request<T>('PATCH', path, payload, options),
  del: <T>(path: string, options?: RequestOptions) => request<T>('DELETE', path, undefined, options),
}

/** Builds a query string, dropping empty values so URLs stay readable. */
export function qs(params: Record<string, string | number | boolean | undefined | null>): string {
  const search = new URLSearchParams()
  for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(params)) {
    if (value === undefined || value === null || value === '' || value === false) continue
    search.set(key, String(value))
  }
  const text = search.toString()
  return text ? `?${text}` : ''
}
/**
 * Application state: the operator's configuration, who is signed in, and the
 * colour scheme. Loaded once, refreshed explicitly - configuration and "me"
 * in parallel, because neither needs the other and each is a round trip to
 * Seoul.
 */
import { createContext, useCallback, useContext, useEffect, useMemo, useState, type ReactNode } from 'react'
import { ApiError, api, onServiceDegraded, onUnauthenticated } from '../api/client'
import type { AppConfig, Me } from '../api/types'

export type ColorScheme = 'light' | 'dark'

interface AppState {
  config: AppConfig | null
  me: Me | null
  booting: boolean
  configError: ApiError | null
  /**
   * The service's database is out of reach (or answers came from saved
   * copies): reads may be old and writes will fail until it is back. Cleared
   * by itself once the health check passes again.
   */
  degraded: boolean
  reloadMe(): Promise<Me | null>
  setMe(me: Me | null): void
  colorScheme: ColorScheme
  setColorScheme(scheme: ColorScheme): void
}

const AppContext = createContext<AppState | null>(null)
const SCHEME_KEY = 'in-color-scheme'

function readStored(key: string): string | null {
  try {
    return localStorage.getItem(key)
  } catch {
    return null
  }
}

function systemScheme(): ColorScheme {
  return window.matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches ? 'dark' : 'light'
}

export function AppProvider({ children }: { children: ReactNode }): ReactNode {
  const [config, setConfig] = useState<AppConfig | null>(null)
  const [me, setMe] = useState<Me | null>(null)
  const [booting, setBooting] = useState(true)
  const [configError, setConfigError] = useState<ApiError | null>(null)
  const [degraded, setDegraded] = useState(false)
  const [colorScheme, setSchemeState] = useState<ColorScheme>(() => {
    const stored = readStored(SCHEME_KEY)
    return stored === 'light' || stored === 'dark' ? stored : systemScheme()
  })

  const setColorScheme = useCallback((scheme: ColorScheme) => {
    setSchemeState(scheme)
    try {
      localStorage.setItem(SCHEME_KEY, scheme)
    } catch {
      // storage refused: the choice lasts for this tab
    }
    document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-mantine-color-scheme', scheme)
  }, [])

  const reloadMe = useCallback(async (): Promise<Me | null> => {
    try {
      const next = (await api.get<{ me: Me | null }>('/api/v1/auth/session')).me
      setMe(next)
      return next
    } catch (err) {
      if (err instanceof ApiError && err.isUnauthenticated) {
        setMe(null)
        return null
      }
      throw err
    }
  }, [])

  useEffect(() => {
    let cancelled = false
    void (async () => {
      const [configResult, meResult] = await Promise.allSettled([
        api.get<AppConfig>('/api/v1/meta/config'),
        window.location.pathname.startsWith('/admin')
          ? Promise.resolve({ me: null })
          : api.get<{ me: Me | null }>('/api/v1/auth/session'),
      ])
      if (cancelled) return
      if (configResult.status === 'fulfilled') setConfig(configResult.value)
      else setConfigError(configResult.reason instanceof ApiError ? configResult.reason : null)
      setMe(meResult.status === 'fulfilled' ? meResult.value.me : null)
      setBooting(false)
    })()
    return () => {
      cancelled = true
    }
  }, [])

  useEffect(() => onUnauthenticated(() => setMe(null)), [])

  // One notice for an outage of the database, cleared when it is back: the
  // health check is asked every 30 seconds while it lasts, and on recovery
  // the configuration and the member are loaded again - the configuration may
  // have been a saved copy or missing, and a member whose "who am I" failed
  // during the outage was shown as signed out.
  useEffect(() => onServiceDegraded(() => setDegraded(true)), [])
  useEffect(() => {
    if (!degraded) return
    let stopped = false
    const timer = window.setInterval(() => {
      void fetch('/api/v1/health', { cache: 'no-store', credentials: 'omit' })
        .then(async (response) => {
          if (stopped || !response.ok) return
          setDegraded(false)
          const next = await api.get<AppConfig>('/api/v1/meta/config').catch(() => null)
          if (next) {
            setConfig(next)
            setConfigError(null)
          }
          await reloadMe().catch(() => null)
        })
        .catch(() => undefined)
    }, 30_000)
    return () => {
      stopped = true
      window.clearInterval(timer)
    }
  }, [degraded, reloadMe])

  useEffect(() => {
    document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-mantine-color-scheme', colorScheme)
  }, [colorScheme])

  const value = useMemo<AppState>(
    () => ({ config, me, booting, configError, degraded, reloadMe, setMe, colorScheme, setColorScheme }),
    [config, me, booting, configError, degraded, reloadMe, colorScheme, setColorScheme],
  )
  return <AppContext.Provider value={value}>{children}</AppContext.Provider>
}

export function useApp(): AppState {
  const value = useContext(AppContext)
  if (!value) throw new Error('useApp must be used inside AppProvider')
  return value
}

export function useConfig(): AppConfig {
  const { config } = useApp()
  if (!config) throw new Error('config is not loaded yet')
  return config
}

/** Where a signed-in participant stands: no profile yet, unfinished, or ready. */
export type Stage = 'none' | 'draft' | 'ready' | 'paused' | 'hidden'

export function stageOf(me: Me | null): Stage {
  const state = me?.participant?.state
  if (!state) return 'none'
  if (state === 'active') return 'ready'
  return state as Stage
}

export function isParticipant(me: Me | null): boolean {
  return Boolean(me?.roles.includes('member'))
}

export function isResearcher(me: Me | null): boolean {
  return (me?.orgs.length ?? 0) > 0
}

export function isAdmin(scopes: string[] | undefined): boolean {
  return (scopes ?? []).some((scope) => scope.startsWith('admin:'))
}
/**
 * Data loading for a screen.
 *
 * Deliberately small: a loader, a reload, and the three states a screen has to
 * render differently - loading, failed, and empty. Written as its own hook so
 * every screen handles a failure the same way instead of some silently showing
 * an empty list (section 21: 저장 실패를 성공 화면으로 표시하지 않는다).
 */
import { useCallback, useEffect, useRef, useState } from 'react'
import { ApiError } from '../api/client'

export interface AsyncState<T> {
  data: T | null
  error: ApiError | null
  loading: boolean
  /** True only for the first load, so a refresh does not blank the screen. */
  initial: boolean
  reload(): Promise<void>
  setData(next: T | null): void
}

export function useAsync<T>(
  loader: (signal: AbortSignal) => Promise<T>,
  deps: readonly unknown[] = [],
): AsyncState<T> {
  const [data, setData] = useState<T | null>(null)
  const [error, setError] = useState<ApiError | null>(null)
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true)
  const [initial, setInitial] = useState(true)
  const controllerRef = useRef<AbortController | null>(null)

  const run = useCallback(async () => {
    controllerRef.current?.abort()
    const controller = new AbortController()
    controllerRef.current = controller
    setLoading(true)
    try {
      const next = await loader(controller.signal)
      if (controller.signal.aborted) return
      setData(next)
      setError(null)
    } catch (err) {
      if (err instanceof DOMException && err.name === 'AbortError') return
      setError(
        err instanceof ApiError
          ? err
          : new ApiError({ status: 0, code: 'unknown', message: '불러오지 못했습니다.' }),
      )
    } finally {
      if (!controller.signal.aborted) {
        setLoading(false)
        setInitial(false)
      }
    }
    // The dependency list is this hook's contract with its caller, so it is
    // deliberately a value rather than a literal and the rule cannot check it.
    // eslint-disable-next-line react-hooks/exhaustive-deps
  }, deps)

  useEffect(() => {
    void run()
    return () => controllerRef.current?.abort()
  }, [run])

  return { data, error, loading, initial, reload: run, setData }
}

/** Runs a one-off action, tracking pending state and the field errors. */
export function useAction<Args extends unknown[], Result>(
  action: (...args: Args) => Promise<Result>,
): {
  run(...args: Args): Promise<Result | undefined>
  pending: boolean
  error: ApiError | null
  reset(): void
} {
  const [pending, setPending] = useState(false)
  const [error, setError] = useState<ApiError | null>(null)
  const inFlight = useRef(false)

  const run = useCallback(
    async (...args: Args): Promise<Result | undefined> => {
      // Guards the double click at the source, not only in the UI (section 21).
      if (inFlight.current) return undefined
      inFlight.current = true
      setPending(true)
      setError(null)
      try {
        return await action(...args)
      } catch (err) {
        setError(
          err instanceof ApiError
            ? err
            : new ApiError({ status: 0, code: 'unknown', message: '처리하지 못했습니다.' }),
        )
        return undefined
      } finally {
        inFlight.current = false
        setPending(false)
      }
    },
    [action],
  )

  return { run, pending, error, reset: () => setError(null) }
}
/**
 * Text normalisation and display helpers.
 *
 * Content is always stored and returned as plain text and rendered as text by
 * the client (COMM-03) - there is no HTML sanitiser here because no HTML is
 * ever rendered.
 */

/** Lowercase, trimmed e-mail used for uniqueness and lookups (COMP-02). */
export function normalizeEmail(email: string): string {
  return email.trim().toLowerCase()
}

/**
 * The mailbox an address delivers to, for "one mailbox, one verification".
 *
 * Corporate mail (Google Workspace, Microsoft 365 and most others) delivers
 * name+anything@company.com to name@company.com. Keyed on the address as
 * typed, one employee could verify any number of accounts at their company -
 * enough to open a company lounge alone or to stack reviews. The tag is
 * dropped for the uniqueness key only; mail still goes to the address given.
 */
export function mailboxKey(email: string): string {
  const normal = normalizeEmail(email)
  const at = normal.lastIndexOf('@')
  if (at <= 0) return normal
  const local = normal.slice(0, at).split('+')[0] || normal.slice(0, at)
  return `${local}@${normal.slice(at + 1)}`
}

/** Domain part of an e-mail, lowercased. Empty string when malformed. */
export function emailDomain(email: string): string {
  const at = email.lastIndexOf('@')
  if (at < 0) return ''
  return email.slice(at + 1).trim().toLowerCase()
}

/** Masks an address for display back to its own owner: `ho**@ex*****.com`. */
export function maskEmail(email: string | null | undefined): string {
  // An account signed in through a provider that gives no address has none;
  // '***' would read as a hidden address rather than an absent one.
  if (!email) return ''
  const at = email.lastIndexOf('@')
  if (at <= 0) return '***'
  const local = email.slice(0, at)
  const domain = email.slice(at + 1)
  const keepLocal = Math.min(2, local.length)
  const dot = domain.lastIndexOf('.')
  const host = dot > 0 ? domain.slice(0, dot) : domain
  const tld = dot > 0 ? domain.slice(dot) : ''
  const keepHost = Math.min(2, host.length)
  return `${local.slice(0, keepLocal)}${'*'.repeat(Math.max(local.length - keepLocal, 1))}` +
    `@${host.slice(0, keepHost)}${'*'.repeat(Math.max(host.length - keepHost, 1))}${tld}`
}

/** Protocols a link in user content may use when the client makes it clickable. */
const ALLOWED_LINK_PROTOCOLS = new Set(['http:', 'https:'])

/** True when a URL found in user text is safe to render as a link (COMM-03). */
export function isSafeLink(raw: string): boolean {
  try {
    const url = new URL(raw)
    if (!ALLOWED_LINK_PROTOCOLS.has(url.protocol)) return false
    // Block the metadata address and obvious private ranges so a rendered link
    // cannot be used to probe internal networks from a member's browser.
    const host = url.hostname
    if (host === '169.254.169.254' || host === 'metadata.google.internal') return false
    return true
  } catch {
    return false
  }
}

/** Collapses runs of blank lines so a post cannot push the feed around. */
export function tidyBody(text: string): string {
  return text.replace(/\r\n?/g, '\n').replace(/\n{4,}/g, '\n\n\n').trimEnd()
}

/** Short excerpt for lists and notifications. */
export function excerpt(text: string, max = 120): string {
  const flat = text.replace(/\s+/g, ' ').trim()
  const chars = [...flat]
  return chars.length <= max ? flat : `${chars.slice(0, max).join('')}...`
}

const ALIAS_ADJECTIVES = [
  '조용한', '성실한', '느긋한', '부지런한', '소심한', '명랑한', '다정한', '씩씩한',
  '차분한', '엉뚱한', '솔직한', '눈치빠른', '덤덤한', '친절한', '무던한', '야무진',
]
const ALIAS_NOUNS = [
  '고양이', '너구리', '참새', '수달', '두루미', '다람쥐', '고라니', '올빼미',
  '청개구리', '해달', '물범', '까치', '토끼', '오리', '살쾡이', '족제비',
]

/**
 * A per-thread display alias. Random, not derived from the account, so two
 * aliases in different threads cannot be linked back to one member (PRIV-02).
 */
export function randomAlias(): string {
  const adjective = ALIAS_ADJECTIVES[Math.floor(Math.random() * ALIAS_ADJECTIVES.length)]
  const noun = ALIAS_NOUNS[Math.floor(Math.random() * ALIAS_NOUNS.length)]
  const suffix = Math.floor(Math.random() * 900 + 100)
  return `${adjective} ${noun} ${suffix}`
}

/** A trade nickname suggestion for a new market profile. */
export function suggestNickname(): string {
  const noun = ALIAS_NOUNS[Math.floor(Math.random() * ALIAS_NOUNS.length)]
  return `${noun}${Math.floor(Math.random() * 9000 + 1000)}`
}

/**
 * Extra digits for a nickname that keeps colliding. The first suggestions draw
 * from four digits, which is pleasant to read and runs out; this widens the
 * space without making every nickname ugly.
 */
export function randomDigits(count: number): string {
  let out = ''
  for (let i = 0; i < count; i++) out += String(Math.floor(Math.random() * 10))
  return out
}

/**
 * Picks the Korean particle that fits the word in front of it.
 *
 * Writing "이(가)" and letting the reader sort it out marks a sentence as
 * machine output, which is the opposite of what an automated post needs.
 *
 * A Hangul syllable encodes its final consonant in its code point: subtract
 * the block start and a remainder of zero means there is none. Trailing
 * brackets, quotes and punctuation are skipped, because a filing name ends
 * ")" or "」" far more often than it ends in a syllable and the particle
 * belongs to the last word, not to the bracket.
 */
export function koreanParticle(word: string, withFinal: string, withoutFinal: string): string {
  for (const char of [...word.trim()].reverse()) {
    const code = char.codePointAt(0) ?? 0
    if (code >= 0xac00 && code <= 0xd7a3) {
      return (code - 0xac00) % 28 === 0 ? withoutFinal : withFinal
    }
    // Digits read aloud in Korean, so they decide the particle themselves.
    if (char >= '0' && char <= '9') {
      // 1, 3, 6, 7, 8, 0 end in a consonant when spoken (일 삼 육 칠 팔 영).
      return '136780'.includes(char) ? withFinal : withoutFinal
    }
  }
  return withoutFinal
}

/** Korean-aware character count (code points, not UTF-16 units). */
export function charCount(text: string): number {
  return [...text].length
}

/** Hash-friendly client fingerprint fragments; never stored raw (SEC-05). */
export function clientIpFrom(request: Request, trustProxy: boolean): string {
  if (!trustProxy) return ''
  const headers = request.headers
  return (
    headers.get('cf-connecting-ip') ??
    headers.get('x-real-ip') ??
    (headers.get('x-forwarded-for') ?? '').split(',')[0]?.trim() ??
    ''
  )
}
/**
 * Time helpers. Everything is stored and compared in UTC; Korean local time is
 * a presentation concern, used for the lunch/after-work windows and for the
 * day boundary that daily quotas reset on (ITEM-03, COMM-07).
 */

export const KST_OFFSET_MINUTES = 9 * 60
const MINUTE = 60_000
const HOUR = 60 * MINUTE
const DAY = 24 * HOUR

export const ms = { minute: MINUTE, hour: HOUR, day: DAY } as const

export function now(): Date {
  return new Date()
}

export function plus(base: Date, amountMs: number): Date {
  return new Date(base.getTime() + amountMs)
}

export function minutes(n: number): number {
  return n * MINUTE
}

export function hours(n: number): number {
  return n * HOUR
}

export function days(n: number): number {
  return n * DAY
}

/** Wall-clock parts in Korea for a given instant. */
export function kstParts(at: Date): { y: number; m: number; d: number; hh: number; mm: number } {
  const shifted = new Date(at.getTime() + KST_OFFSET_MINUTES * MINUTE)
  return {
    y: shifted.getUTCFullYear(),
    m: shifted.getUTCMonth() + 1,
    d: shifted.getUTCDate(),
    hh: shifted.getUTCHours(),
    mm: shifted.getUTCMinutes(),
  }
}

/** Start of the Korean calendar day containing `at`, as a UTC instant. */
export function kstDayStart(at: Date): Date {
  const p = kstParts(at)
  return new Date(Date.UTC(p.y, p.m - 1, p.d) - KST_OFFSET_MINUTES * MINUTE)
}

/** `YYYY-MM-DD` in Korean local time, used as a daily quota window key. */
export function kstDateKey(at: Date): string {
  const p = kstParts(at)
  return `${p.y}-${String(p.m).padStart(2, '0')}-${String(p.d).padStart(2, '0')}`
}

/** Start of the minute containing `at`, used as a per-minute quota window. */
export function minuteStart(at: Date): Date {
  return new Date(Math.floor(at.getTime() / MINUTE) * MINUTE)
}

/** True when two half-open intervals overlap (ITEM-05). */
export function overlaps(aStart: Date, aEnd: Date, bStart: Date, bEnd: Date): boolean {
  return aStart.getTime() < bEnd.getTime() && bStart.getTime() < aEnd.getTime()
}

/**
 * Resolves an `HH:MM` policy window (e.g. lunch 11:30-14:00) to an absolute
 * UTC interval on the Korean day containing `reference`.
 */
export function kstWindowOn(reference: Date, from: string, to: string): { start: Date; end: Date } {
  const dayStart = kstDayStart(reference)
  return {
    start: plus(dayStart, parseClock(from)),
    end: plus(dayStart, parseClock(to)),
  }
}

function parseClock(value: string): number {
  const [h = '0', m = '0'] = value.split(':')
  const hh = Math.min(Math.max(Number.parseInt(h, 10) || 0, 0), 47)
  const mm = Math.min(Math.max(Number.parseInt(m, 10) || 0, 0), 59)
  return hh * HOUR + mm * MINUTE
}

/** Human Korean date-time for notification text and admin lists. */
export function formatKst(at: Date): string {
  const p = kstParts(at)
  return `${p.y}.${String(p.m).padStart(2, '0')}.${String(p.d).padStart(2, '0')} ` +
    `${String(p.hh).padStart(2, '0')}:${String(p.mm).padStart(2, '0')}`
}

/**
 * Exponential backoff with jitter for job retries (JOB-03).
 *
 * The jitter is applied before the cap, not after: jittering a capped value
 * can land above the cap, which makes the cap something other than a cap.
 */
export function backoffMs(attempt: number, baseMs = 30_000, capMs = 6 * HOUR): number {
  const exponential = baseMs * 2 ** Math.max(attempt - 1, 0)
  const jittered = exponential * (0.75 + Math.random() * 0.5)
  return Math.floor(Math.min(jittered, capMs))
}
/**
 * A small read cache in front of the API.
 *
 * Every server call from Korea is a trip to Los Angeles and on to Seoul, so a
 * screen that asks again for what it was told a moment ago - the room list on
 * every visit to the feed, the unread counts on every navigation, a company
 * page opened twice - pays the whole trip for nothing. Reads that opt in are
 * kept for a short, per-call time, identical reads in flight are merged into
 * one, and a link the reader is about to open can be fetched ahead.
 *
 * Correctness comes first, by three rules:
 *   - any write by this reader (POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE that succeeds) empties
 *     the cache, so what they just did is never hidden behind an old copy;
 *   - signing in or out, or any 401, empties it, so one person's data is never
 *     shown to the next;
 *   - a read that was in flight when the cache was emptied is not stored, so
 *     an answer from before a write cannot come back as if it were after it.
 * Nothing is cached unless the call asks, and nothing is kept past its age.
 */

interface Entry {
  at: number
  value?: unknown
  promise?: Promise<unknown>
}

const entries = new Map<string, Entry>()
let generation = 0

/** Drops everything. Called on every write, sign-in, sign-out and 401. */
export function invalidateAll(): void {
  generation += 1
  entries.clear()
  earlyReads()?.clear()
}

interface EarlyRead {
  at: number
  response: Promise<Response>
}

/** Reads public/boot.js started before the app loaded, keyed by path. */
function earlyReads(): { take(path: string): EarlyRead | undefined; clear(): void } | null {
  const holder = window as unknown as { __yuEarly?: Record<string, EarlyRead> }
  const all = holder.__yuEarly
  if (!all) return null
  return {
    take(path) {
      const entry = all[path]
      delete all[path]
      return entry
    },
    clear() {
      holder.__yuEarly = {}
    },
  }
}

/** How long an early read may stand in for the app's own request. */
const EARLY_MAX_AGE = 10_000

/**
 * The response to a read boot.js already started for `path`, if one is there
 * and young - handed over once. Undefined means: ask the server yourself.
 */
export function takeEarly(path: string): Promise<Response> | undefined {
  const entry = earlyReads()?.take(path)
  if (!entry || Date.now() - entry.at > EARLY_MAX_AGE) return undefined
  return entry.response
}

/** The cached value if it is younger than `maxAge`, else undefined. */
export function peek<T>(key: string, maxAge: number): T | undefined {
  const entry = entries.get(key)
  if (!entry || entry.value === undefined) return undefined
  return Date.now() - entry.at <= maxAge ? (entry.value as T) : undefined
}

/**
 * `load` once per `maxAge` per key. Concurrent callers share one request;
 * failures are not remembered, so a retry really retries.
 */
export function remember<T>(key: string, maxAge: number, load: () => Promise<T>): Promise<T> {
  const fresh = peek<T>(key, maxAge)
  if (fresh !== undefined) return Promise.resolve(fresh)
  const existing = entries.get(key)
  if (existing?.promise) return existing.promise as Promise<T>

  const started = generation
  const promise = load().then(
    (value) => {
      // Emptied while this was on the wire: the answer may predate a write.
      if (generation === started) entries.set(key, { at: Date.now(), value })
      else entries.delete(key)
      return value
    },
    (error: unknown) => {
      entries.delete(key)
      throw error
    },
  )
  entries.set(key, { at: Date.now(), promise })
  return promise
}

/** Forgets one key, for a screen whose reload button must really reload. */
export function forget(key: string): void {
  entries.delete(key)
}

/** How long the detail screens keep what they read; shared with prefetching. */
export const POST_MAX_AGE = 15_000
export const COMPANY_MAX_AGE = 60_000

/**
 * Settings service: reads the operator-edited values, falling back to the
 * registry defaults, and writes them with validation plus a change record.
 *
 * Secret-marked values are sealed with the dedicated secrets key before they
 * touch the table and are never returned by a read API (spec section 22).
 */
import type { Database } from '../db.js'
import type { Env } from '../env.js'
import { open, seal } from '../util/crypto.js'
import {
  SETTINGS,
  SETTING_KEYS,
  coerceSetting,
  defaultValues,
  type SettingIssue,
  type SettingKey,
  type SettingValues,
} from './registry.js'

/** How long a loaded snapshot is reused within one runtime instance. */
const CACHE_TTL_MS = 10_000

interface Snapshot {
  values: SettingValues
  loadedAt: number
}

/**
 * Snapshots shared by every Settings object in this runtime instance, by
 * database.
 *
 * On Workers the services are built again for every request, so a snapshot
 * held on the instance was never read twice: every request paid for loading
 * the whole table, before it had done anything, from a database on the other
 * side of the Pacific. Only the finished snapshot is shared. A load in flight
 * stays with the request that started it, since a request must not wait on
 * I/O another request owns.
 */
const shared = new Map<string, Snapshot>()

export class Settings {
  private snapshot: Snapshot | null = null
  private inflight: Promise<Snapshot> | null = null

  constructor(
    private readonly db: Database,
    private readonly env: Env,
  ) {}

  /** All effective values. Secrets are decrypted; do not pass this to a client. */
  async all(): Promise<SettingValues> {
    return (await this.load()).values
  }

  /** One typed value. */
  async get<K extends SettingKey>(key: K): Promise<SettingValues[K]> {
    const values = await this.all()
    return values[key]
  }

  /** Several values at once, avoiding repeated snapshot lookups. */
  async pick<K extends SettingKey>(...keys: K[]): Promise<Pick<SettingValues, K>> {
    const values = await this.all()
    const out = {} as Pick<SettingValues, K>
    for (const key of keys) out[key] = values[key]
    return out
  }

  /** Values safe to serve to any client: secrets replaced by a presence flag. */
  async publicView(): Promise<Record<string, unknown>> {
    const values = await this.all()
    const out: Record<string, unknown> = {}
    for (const key of SETTING_KEYS) {
      const spec = SETTINGS[key]
      out[key] = spec.secret === true ? (values[key] ? '설정됨' : '') : values[key]
    }
    return out
  }

  /** Drops the cached snapshot so the next read goes to the database. */
  invalidate(): void {
    this.snapshot = null
    shared.delete(this.db.key)
  }

  /**
   * Applies a batch of changes. Every key is validated against the registry
   * first, so a single bad field rejects the whole batch instead of leaving
   * half-applied policy (OPS-06).
   */
  async update(
    patch: Record<string, unknown>,
    actor: { accountId: string; roles: readonly string[] },
  ): Promise<{ applied: string[]; issues: SettingIssue[] }> {
    const issues: SettingIssue[] = []
    const coerced: { key: SettingKey; value: unknown; secret: boolean }[] = []

    for (const [key, raw] of Object.entries(patch)) {
      const result = coerceSetting(key, raw)
      if (!result.ok) {
        issues.push(result.issue)
        continue
      }
      const spec = SETTINGS[key as SettingKey]
      coerced.push({ key: key as SettingKey, value: result.value, secret: spec.secret === true })
    }
    if (issues.length > 0) return { applied: [], issues }

    const current = await this.all()
    const applied: string[] = []

    await this.db.internalAs({ accountId: actor.accountId, roles: actor.roles }, async (sql) => {
      for (const entry of coerced) {
        const before = current[entry.key]
        // A blank secret means "leave as is" so the masked field can round-trip.
        if (entry.secret && entry.value === '') continue
        if (!entry.secret && JSON.stringify(before) === JSON.stringify(entry.value)) continue

        const stored = entry.secret
          ? await seal(this.env.keys.secrets, String(entry.value), `setting:${entry.key}`)
          : entry.value

        await sql`
          INSERT INTO insight.settings (skey, value, is_secret, updated_at, updated_by, version)
          VALUES (${entry.key}, ${sql.json(stored as never)}, ${entry.secret}, now(), ${actor.accountId}, 1)
          ON CONFLICT (skey) DO UPDATE
            SET value = EXCLUDED.value,
                is_secret = EXCLUDED.is_secret,
                updated_at = now(),
                updated_by = EXCLUDED.updated_by,
                version = insight.settings.version + 1`

        await sql`
          INSERT INTO insight_priv.settings_history (skey, before_val, after_val, actor_id)
          VALUES (
            ${entry.key},
            ${sql.json((entry.secret ? '***' : (before ?? null)) as never)},
            ${sql.json((entry.secret ? '***' : entry.value) as never)},
            ${actor.accountId})`

        applied.push(entry.key)
      }
    })

    this.invalidate()
    return { applied, issues }
  }

  /** Change history for one key, for the admin audit view. */
  async history(key: string, limit = 50): Promise<
    { skey: string; before: unknown; after: unknown; actorId: string | null; at: string }[]
  > {
    const rows = await this.db.internal(
      async (sql) => sql<{ skey: string; before_val: unknown; after_val: unknown; actor_id: string | null; created_at: Date }[]>`
        SELECT skey, before_val, after_val, actor_id, created_at
        FROM insight_priv.settings_history
        WHERE skey = ${key}
        ORDER BY created_at DESC
        LIMIT ${Math.min(Math.max(limit, 1), 200)}`,
    )
    return rows.map((r) => ({
      skey: r.skey,
      before: r.before_val,
      after: r.after_val,
      actorId: r.actor_id,
      at: r.created_at.toISOString(),
    }))
  }

  /** Writes any missing default row. Safe to call on every boot. */
  async ensureDefaults(): Promise<number> {
    const defaults = defaultValues()
    return this.db.internal(async (sql) => {
      const existing = new Set(
        (await sql<{ skey: string }[]>`SELECT skey FROM insight.settings`).map((r) => r.skey),
      )
      let written = 0
      for (const key of SETTING_KEYS) {
        if (existing.has(key)) continue
        const spec = SETTINGS[key]
        if (spec.secret === true) continue // never seed an empty secret row
        await sql`
          INSERT INTO insight.settings (skey, value, is_secret)
          VALUES (${key}, ${sql.json(defaults[key] as never)}, false)
          ON CONFLICT (skey) DO NOTHING`
        written++
      }
      return written
    })
  }

  private async load(): Promise<Snapshot> {
    const cached = this.snapshot ?? shared.get(this.db.key) ?? null
    if (cached && Date.now() - cached.loadedAt < CACHE_TTL_MS) return cached
    if (this.inflight) return this.inflight

    this.inflight = this.readAll()
      .then((snapshot) => {
        this.snapshot = snapshot
        shared.set(this.db.key, snapshot)
        return snapshot
      })
      .finally(() => {
        this.inflight = null
      })
    return this.inflight
  }

  private async readAll(): Promise<Snapshot> {
    const values = defaultValues()
    // Readable by anyone under its policy, so one statement with no
    // transaction around it (Database.read).
    const rows = await this.db.read(
      async (sql) =>
        sql<{ skey: string; value: unknown; is_secret: boolean }[]>`
          SELECT skey, value, is_secret FROM insight.settings`,
    )

    for (const row of rows) {
      if (!(row.skey in SETTINGS)) continue
      const key = row.skey as SettingKey
      if (row.is_secret) {
        const plain = await open(this.env.keys.secrets, String(row.value ?? ''), `setting:${key}`)
        // A secret that will not open means the key rotated without re-encrypting.
        // Fall back to empty rather than leaking ciphertext into application logic.
        ;(values as Record<string, unknown>)[key] = plain ?? ''
        continue
      }
      const check = coerceSetting(key, row.value)
      ;(values as Record<string, unknown>)[key] = check.ok ? check.value : SETTINGS[key].default
    }
    return { values, loadedAt: Date.now() }
  }
}
/**
 * The database out of reach (2026-10-14: six hours through the shared pool).
 *
 * What has to hold: a call to an unreachable database fails as db_unavailable
 * (503, Retry-After), quickly; the next calls in the isolate fail at once
 * without trying; after the wait one probe goes through; and the API answers
 * "점검 중" with 503 rather than a 500. (This service draws no pages on the
 * server; the saved copies of its public answers are functions/[[path]].ts.)
 */
import { createServer, type Server } from 'node:net'
import { afterAll, afterEach, beforeAll, describe, expect, it, vi } from 'vitest'
import { Database, breakerKeyFor, databaseBreaker, resetDatabaseBreakers } from '../db.js'
import { AppError, dbUnavailable, isDatabaseUnreachable } from '../errors.js'
import { alertOperator } from '../http/pipeline.js'
import { errorResponse } from '../http/respond.js'

// Nothing listens on port 1: the connection is refused at once.
const NOWHERE = 'postgres://nobody:nothing@127.0.0.1:1/none'

// A "database" that accepts a connection and drops it - how the pool behaved
// on 2026-10-14 (write CONNECTION_CLOSED) - counting every attempt, so a test
// can tell "failed fast without trying" from "tried and failed fast".
let dropper: Server
let dropped = 0
let DROPPING = ''
// And one that accepts and never answers - the slow end of the same outage.
let hole: Server
let SILENT = ''
const held = new Set<import('node:net').Socket>()
beforeAll(async () => {
  hole = createServer((socket) => {
    held.add(socket)
    socket.on('data', () => undefined)
  })
  await new Promise<void>((resolve) => hole.listen(0, '127.0.0.1', resolve))
  const holeAddress = hole.address()
  if (!holeAddress || typeof holeAddress === 'string') throw new Error('no port')
  SILENT = `postgres://nobody:nothing@127.0.0.1:${holeAddress.port}/none`

  dropper = createServer((socket) => {
    dropped++
    socket.destroy()
  })
  await new Promise<void>((resolve) => dropper.listen(0, '127.0.0.1', resolve))
  const address = dropper.address()
  if (!address || typeof address === 'string') throw new Error('no port')
  DROPPING = `postgres://nobody:nothing@127.0.0.1:${address.port}/none`
})
afterAll(async () => {
  await new Promise<void>((resolve) => dropper.close(() => resolve()))
  for (const socket of held) socket.destroy()
  await new Promise<void>((resolve) => hole.close(() => resolve()))
})

afterEach(() => {
  vi.restoreAllMocks()
  resetDatabaseBreakers()
})

async function failure(promise: Promise<unknown>): Promise<AppError> {
  try {
    await promise
  } catch (err) {
    if (err instanceof AppError) return err
    throw new Error(`expected an AppError, got ${String(err)}`)
  }
  throw new Error('expected a failure')
